"""Names the A5 kernel translation unit declares, which printed CCE and PTO ISA identifiers avoid (RFC-0007 §1).

`simt::launch<f>` names no single function when `f` also names another visible function, and a macro rewrites any
identifier. These are the ordinary spellings of the functions declared at global scope or through `using namespace
ascrip`, and of the macros, in the real compile of a printed one-launch kernel captured on the A5 host (CANN 9.2.0,
bisheng clang 15.0.5, glibc 2.39, libstdc++ 13), less that kernel's entry and per-parameter -D macros; C++-reserved
spellings are respelled by rule (`cpp.kernel_reserved`). `printf` is measured: its launch did not compile, although
that translation unit declares no global `printf` (I031).
"""

